st","Альтернатива ngrok","Самостоятельный хостинг","Активная разработка","Подробные спецификации в issues"],"ar":["تم تطويره في Rust","بديل ngrok","المضيف الذاتي","قيد التطوير النشط","مواصفات مفصلة في القضايا"]},"keywords":{"zh":["zgrok开发者","自托管ngrok替代品","Rust开发","如何使用zgrok","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrok安装","zgrok设置指南","ngrok替代品","自托管工具"],"ja":["zgrok開発者","セルフホストngrok代替品","Rust開発","zgrokの使い方","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrokインストール","zgrok設定ガイド","ngrok代替品","セルフホストツール"],"ko":["zgrok 개발자","자체 호스팅 ngrok 대안","러스트 개발","zgrok 사용법","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrok 설치","zgrok 설정 가이드","ngrok 대안","자체 호스팅 도구"],"es":["alternativa a ngrok","herramientas de AI","desarrollo en Rust","cómo usar zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","instalación de zgrok-developer"],"fr":["alternative à ngrok","outils d''Agents d''IA","développement en Rust","comment utiliser zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","installation de zgrok-developer"],"de":["Alternative zu ngrok","KI-Tools","Entwicklung in Rust","wie man zgrok-developer verwendet","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","Installation von zgrok-developer"],"pt":["zgrok-developer","ngrok alternative","ferramenta de desenvolvimento em Rust","self-hosted","como usar zgrok-developer","o que é zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","instalar zgrok-developer"],"ru":["zgrok-developer","ИИ Агенты","альтернатива ngrok","инструмент разработки на Rust","самостоятельный хостинг","как использовать zgrok-developer","что такое zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","установка zgrok-developer"],"ar":["zgrok-developer","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل ngrok","أداة تطوير في Rust","المضيف الذاتي","كيفية استخدام zgrok-developer","ما هو zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer مقابل ngrok","تثبيت zgrok-developer"]}},"owner":"copyleftdev","repo":"zgrok","repoPath":"copyleftdev/zgrok","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.688Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zgrok-developer","description":"Develop zgrok tunnel service following project conventions, issue specs, and Rust best practices. Use when implementing features, fixing bugs, or reviewing code in this repository.","bodyPreview":"# zgrok Developer Skill\n\n## ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENTS\n\n**These are non-negotiable. Violating these is a failure condition.**\n\n### No Tutorial Comments\n\nNEVER add comments explaining what code does. Code must be self-documenting.\n\nAllowed comments:\n- `///` doc comments for public API\n- `// TODO:` or `// FIXME:`\n- `// SAFETY:` for unsafe blocks\n- Brief \"why\" explanations for non-obvious decisions\n\nForbidden:\n- `// Initialize the counter`\n- `// Loop through items`\n- `// Check if value is null`\n- Any co","body":"# zgrok Developer Skill\n\n## ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENTS\n\n**These are non-negotiable. Violating these is a failure condition.**\n\n### No Tutorial Comments\n\nNEVER add comments explaining what code does. Code must be self-documenting.\n\nAllowed comments:\n- `///` doc comments for public API\n- `// TODO:` or `// FIXME:`\n- `// SAFETY:` for unsafe blocks\n- Brief \"why\" explanations for non-obvious decisions\n\nForbidden:\n- `// Initialize the counter`\n- `// Loop through items`\n- `// Check if value is null`\n- Any comment that restates what the code does\n\n### Branch Workflow (Mandatory)\n\nFor EVERY issue:\n\n1. `git checkout main && git pull origin main`\n2. `git checkout -b feat/ZGROK-XXX-description`\n3. Implement all acceptance criteria\n4. `cargo fmt && cargo clippy -- -D warnings && cargo test`\n5. `git add -A && git commit -m \"feat(component): ZGROK-XXX - title\"`\n6. `git push -u origin feat/ZGROK-XXX-description`\n7. `gh pr create --fill`\n8. Self-review the diff\n9. `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`\n10. `git checkout main && git pull origin main`\n11. Report completion, await next issue\n\n**NEVER leave PRs open. NEVER work multiple issues. NEVER skip steps.**\n\n## Overview\n\nzgrok is a self-hosted ngrok alternative. This skill encodes project-specific knowledge for effective development.\n\n## Issue-Driven Development\n\nAll work traces to issues in `.github/issues/`. Each issue contains:\n\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: Testable Given/When/Then statements\n- **State Machines**: For stateful components (connections, streams)\n- **Technical Context**: Exact crates, files, data structures to use\n- **Dependencies**: What must exist before this can be implemented\n\n### Reading an Issue\n\n```bash\ncat .github/issues/stories/protocol/ZGROK-010-frame-types.json | jq\n```\n\n### Checking Dependencies\n\n```bash\ncat .github/issues/_index.json | jq ''.dependency_graph[\"ZGROK-012\"]''\n```\n\n## Architecture Principles\n\n1. **Async-first**: Everything uses Tokio. No blocking in async context.\n2. **Protocol-agnostic core**: The multiplexer works over any `AsyncRead + AsyncWrite`.\n3. **Graceful degradation**: Connection loss → reconnect, not crash.\n4. **Observable**: Every component emits tracing spans and metrics.\n\n## Code Patterns\n\n### Error Handling\n\n```rust\n// Library crates: use thiserror\n#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\npub enum ProtocolError {\n    #[error(\"invalid frame type: {0}\")]\n    InvalidFrameType(u8),\n    #[error(\"stream {0} not found\")]\n    StreamNotFound(u32),\n    #[error(\"io error: {0}\")]\n    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),\n}\n\n// Binary crates: use anyhow\nfn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Tracing\n\n```rust\nuse tracing::{debug, info, instrument, warn};\n\n#[instrument(skip(stream), fields(stream_id = %stream.id()))]\nasync fn handle_stream(stream: Stream) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    info!(\"processing stream\");\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### State Machines\n\nImplement exactly as specified in issue `state_machine` field:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum StreamState {\n    Open,\n    HalfClosedLocal,\n    HalfClosedRemote,\n    Closed,\n}\n\nimpl StreamState {\n    pub fn can_send(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::Open | Self::HalfClosedRemote)\n    }\n    \n    pub fn can_recv(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::Open | Self::HalfClosedLocal)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n1. **Unit tests**: Per-function, alongside code\n2. **Property tests**: Protocol codec with `proptest`\n3. **Integration tests**: Full tunnel flow in `tests/`\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n    \n    #[test]\n    fn test_frame_roundtrip() {\n        // Maps to AC: Given valid frame, When encoded then decoded, Then equals original\n        let frame = Frame::Data { stream_id: 1, payload: b\"hello\".to_vec() };\n        let encoded = frame.encode();\n        let decoded = Frame::decode(&encoded).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(frame, decoded);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## File Organization\n\n```\ncrates/\n├── zgrok-protocol/src/\n│   ├── lib.rs          # Public API, re-exports\n│   ├── frame.rs        # Frame types and codec\n│   ├── codec.rs        # Tokio codec impl\n│   ├── mux.rs          # Stream multiplexer\n│   └── error.rs        # Protocol errors\n├── zgrok-agent/src/\n│   ├── main.rs         # CLI entry\n│   ├── cli.rs          # Clap definitions\n│   ├── tunnel.rs       # Connection management\n│   ├── forwarder.rs    # Local HTTP forwarding\n│   └── tui/            # Terminal UI\n└── zgrok-edge/src/\n    ├── main.rs\n    ├── acceptor.rs     # Agent connection handling\n    ├── router.rs       # Subdomain routing\n    └── bridge.rs       # HTTP-to-tunnel bridging\n```\n\n## Commit Convention\n\n```\nfeat(protocol): ZGROK-010 - define frame types and binary format\nfix(agent): ZGROK-033 - handle reconnection edge case\ntest(edge): ZGROK-054 - add agent acceptor integration tests\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T13:29:54.635Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust Developer Agents needing self-hosted ngrok alternatives with comprehensive code documentation.","zh":"非常适合需要自托管ngrok替代品并具有全面代码文档的Rust开发者代理。","ja":"Rust開発者エージェントが自ホスト型のngrokの代替品を必要とする場合に最適です。包括的なコードドキュメントを提供します。","ko":"자체 호스팅 ngrok 대체품과 포괄적인 코드 문서가 필요한 Rust 개발자 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Rust que necesitan alternativas de ngrok autoalojadas con documentación de código completa.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement Rust nécessitant des alternatives ngrok auto-hébergées avec une documentation de code complète.","de":"Perfekt für Rust-Entwicklungsagenten, die selbstgehostete ngrok-Alternativen mit umfassender Code-Dokumentation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedores Rust que precisam de alternativas de auto-hospedagem do ngrok com documentação de código abrangente.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков Rust, которым необходимы альтернативы ngrok с само-хостингом и полной документацией кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مطور الرست الذي يحتاج إلى بدائل ل ngrok ذات استضافة ذاتية مع توثيق شاملة للكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop and deploy a self-hosted ngrok alternative in Rust, utilizing public API documentation with /// doc comments, and ensuring code clarity with brief ''why'' explanations for non-obvious decisions, all while adhering to strict commenting standards and utilizing protocols like ngrok''s tunneling protocol.","zh":"赋予代理开发和部署自托管ngrok替代品的能力，利用公共API文档和///文档注释，确保代码清晰度，并使用类似ngrok的隧道协议，同时遵循严格的注释标准。","ja":"エージェントが自ホスト型のngrokの代替品を開発してデプロイできるようにし、公開されたAPIドキュメントと///ドキュメントコメントを使用してコードの明確性を確保し、ngrokのトンネリングプロトコルなどのプロトコルを使用しながら、厳格なコメント規範に従います。","ko":"에이전트가 자체 호스팅 ngrok 대체품을 개발하고 배포할 수 있도록 하며, 공개 API 문서와 /// 문서 주석을 사용하여 코드의 명확성을 보장하고, ngrok의 터널링 프로토콜과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하면서 엄격한 주석 표준을 준수합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes desarrollar y desplegar una alternativa de ngrok autoalojada en Rust, utilizando la documentación de API pública con comentarios /// doc, y garantizando la claridad del código con breves explicaciones de ''por qué'' para decisiones no obvias, todo mientras se adhiere a estrictas normas de comentarios y se utilizan protocolos como el protocolo de túneles de ngrok.","fr":"Permet aux agents de 