rlagen für einen schnellen Start","Anpassbar, um sich an Ihre Bedürfnisse anzupassen"],"pt":["Arquitetura limpa e simples","Integração com Next.js","Modelo de repositório pronto para uso","Suporte a MCP skills","Desenvolvimento rápido e eficiente"],"ru":["Чистая и простая архитектура","Интеграция с Next.js","Готовый шаблон репозитория","Поддержка MCP skills","Быстрое и эффективное развитие"],"ar":["هندسة نظيفة وبسيطة","التكامل مع Next.js","قالب مخزن جاهز للاستخدام","دعم MCP skills","التطوير السريع والفعال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用Pages Router","什么是Next.js页面路由","Pages Router替代品","Next.js页面路由器教程","Pages Router安装","Next.js页面开发指南"],"ja":["Pages Routerの使い方","Next.jsページルーティングとは","Pages Routerの代替品","Next.jsページルーティングのチュートリアル","Pages Routerのインストール","Next.jsページ開発ガイド"],"ko":["Pages Router 사용법","Next.js 페이지 라우팅이란","Pages Router 대체품","Next.js 페이지 라우팅 튜토리얼","Pages Router 설치","Next.js 페이지 개발 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar pages-router","qué es pages-router","alternativas a pages-router","pages-router vs Next.js","instalación de pages-router","guía de configuración de pages-router","desarrollo de aplicaciones con pages-router"],"fr":["comment utiliser pages-router","qu''est-ce que pages-router","alternatives à pages-router","pages-router vs Next.js","installation de pages-router","guide de configuration de pages-router","développement d''applications avec pages-router"],"de":["wie man pages-router verwendet","was ist pages-router","alternativen zu pages-router","pages-router vs Next.js","installation von pages-router","konfigurationsanleitung für pages-router","entwicklung von anwendungen mit pages-router"],"pt":["como usar pages-router","o que é pages-router","alternativas para Next.js","pages-router vs React","instalar pages-router","guia de configuração do pages-router"],"ru":["как использовать pages-router","что такое pages-router","альтернативы для Next.js","pages-router vs React","установить pages-router","руководство по настройке pages-router"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام pages-router","ما هو pages-router","بديل ل Next.js","pages-router مقابل React","تثبيت pages-router","دليل إعداد pages-router"]}},"owner":"jorggerojas","repo":"next-skeleton-page","repoPath":"jorggerojas/next-skeleton-page","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.825Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pages-router","description":"Work with Next.js Pages Router pages in src/pages/. Use when creating or modifying pages, working with _app.tsx, _document.tsx, or any page components in the Pages Router structure.","bodyPreview":"# Next.js Pages Router\n\n## Structure\n\nThis project uses **Pages Router** exclusively. All pages go in `src/pages/`.\n\n- Regular pages: `src/pages/[filename].tsx` → `/filename` route\n- Dynamic routes: `src/pages/[id]/page.tsx` → `/[id]` route\n- API routes: `src/pages/api/[route].ts` → `/api/[route]` endpoint\n- Special files: `_app.tsx`, `_document.tsx` in `src/pages/`\n\n## Creating Pages\n\n### Basic Page\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/about.tsx\nexport default function About() {\n  return <div>About page</div>;","body":"# Next.js Pages Router\n\n## Structure\n\nThis project uses **Pages Router** exclusively. All pages go in `src/pages/`.\n\n- Regular pages: `src/pages/[filename].tsx` → `/filename` route\n- Dynamic routes: `src/pages/[id]/page.tsx` → `/[id]` route\n- API routes: `src/pages/api/[route].ts` → `/api/[route]` endpoint\n- Special files: `_app.tsx`, `_document.tsx` in `src/pages/`\n\n## Creating Pages\n\n### Basic Page\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/about.tsx\nexport default function About() {\n  return <div>About page</div>;\n}\n```\n\n### Dynamic Route\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/users/[id].tsx\nimport { useRouter } from ''next/router'';\n\nexport default function User() {\n  const router = useRouter();\n  const { id } = router.query;\n  \n  return <div>User {id}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n### Nested Dynamic Route\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/posts/[id]/[slug].tsx\nimport { useRouter } from ''next/router'';\n\nexport default function Post() {\n  const router = useRouter();\n  const { id, slug } = router.query;\n  \n  return <div>Post {id} - {slug}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n## Special Files\n\n### _app.tsx\n\nWraps all pages. Use for:\n\n- Global providers\n- Global styles\n- Layout components\n- Page-level state\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/_app.tsx\nimport \"@/styles/globals.css\";\nimport type { AppProps } from \"next/app\";\n\nexport default function App({ Component, pageProps }: AppProps) {\n  return <Component {...pageProps} />;\n}\n```\n\n### _document.tsx\n\nCustomizes HTML document. Use for:\n\n- `<html>` and `<body>` attributes\n- Custom fonts\n- Analytics scripts\n- Meta tags\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/_document.tsx\nimport { Html, Head, Main, NextScript } from \"next/document\";\n\nexport default function Document() {\n  return (\n    <Html lang=\"en\">\n      <Head />\n      <body className=\"antialiased\">\n        <Main />\n        <NextScript />\n      </body>\n    </Html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Data Fetching\n\n**CRITICAL**: Only pages handle server-side data fetching. Components, hooks, or other files should NOT make server calls directly. All data fetching happens in the page file using `getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`, or `getStaticPaths`.\n\n### getServerSideProps\n\nThe page component goes first, then the data fetching function. **The page component''s Props type MUST be inferred from `getServerSideProps` using `InferGetServerSidePropsType`.**\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/posts/[id].tsx\nimport type { GetServerSideProps, InferGetServerSidePropsType } from \"next\";\nimport { PageLayout } from \"@/components\";\n\nexport const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async (context) => {\n  const { id } = context.params!;\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/posts/${id}`);\n  const post = await res.json();\n  \n  return {\n    props: { post },\n  };\n};\n\n// Type MUST be inferred from getServerSideProps\nexport default function Post({ post }: InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>) {\n  return (\n    <PageLayout\n      title={post.title}\n      description={post.content}\n      canonical={`/posts/${post.id}`}\n    >\n      <div>\n        <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n        <p>{post.content}</p>\n      </div>\n    </PageLayout>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### getStaticProps\n\n**The page component''s Props type MUST be inferred from `getStaticProps` using `InferGetStaticPropsType`.**\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/posts/[id].tsx\nimport type { GetStaticProps, GetStaticPaths, InferGetStaticPropsType } from \"next\";\nimport { PageLayout } from \"@/components\";\n\nexport const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async (context) => {\n  const { id } = context.params!;\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/posts/${id}`);\n  const post = await res.json();\n  \n  return {\n    props: { post },\n    revalidate: 60, // ISR: revalidate every 60 seconds\n  };\n};\n\nexport const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {\n  return {\n    paths: [{ params: { id: ''1'' } }, { params: { id: ''2'' } }],\n    fallback: ''blocking'', // or true, false\n  };\n};\n\n// Type MUST be inferred from getStaticProps\nexport default function Post({ post }: InferGetStaticPropsType<typeof getStaticProps>) {\n  return (\n    <PageLayout\n      title={post.title}\n      description={post.content}\n      canonical={`/posts/${post.id}`}\n    >\n      <div>\n        <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n        <p>{post.content}</p>\n      </div>\n    </PageLayout>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Type Inference\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The page component''s `Props` type **MUST** be inferred from `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps` using `InferGetServerSidePropsType` or `InferGetStaticPropsType`. Do not manually define the Props type.\n\n```tsx\nimport type { GetServerSideProps, InferGetServerSidePropsType } from \"next\";\n\nexport const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async () => {\n  return {\n    props: { post: { id: \"1\", title: \"Hello\" } },\n  };\n};\n\n// Type MUST be inferred from getServerSideProps\nexport default function Post({ post }: InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>) {\n  return <div>{post.title}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n### Using Hooks in Pages\n\nPages can use custom hooks for client-side data fetching, mutations, or other client-side logic. Examples:\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/users.tsx\nimport type { GetServerSideProps, InferGetServerSidePropsType } from \"next\";\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async () => {\n  return { props: { initialUsers: [] } };\n};\n\nexport default function UsersPage({ initialUsers }: InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>) {\n  const { data: users, isLoading } = useUsers();\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      {isLoading ? <p>Loading...</p> : <UserList users={users} />}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/pages/hotels/[id].tsx\nimport type { GetServerSideProps, InferGetServerSidePropsType } from \"next\";\nimport { useHotels } from \"@/hooks/hotels\";\n\nexport const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async (context) => {\n  const { id } = context.params!;\n  return { props: { hotelId: id } };\n};\n\nexport default function HotelPage({ hotelId }: InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>) {\n  const { data: hotel } = useHotels.getById(hotelId);\n  const createMutation = useHotels.create();\n  \n  const handleCreate = () => {\n    createMutation.mutate({ name: \"New Hotel\" });\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{hotel?.name}</h1>\n      <button onClick={handleCreate}>Create Hotel</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Note**: Server-side data fetching (API calls) should only happen in `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps`. Hooks like `useUsers()`, `useHotels()`, `useHotels.create()`, etc., are for client-side data fetching, mutations, or other client-side logic.\n\n## Client-Side Navigation\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from ''next/link'';\nimport { useRouter } from ''next/router'';\n\nexport default function Navigation() {\n  const router = useRouter();\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <Link href=\"/about\">About</Link>\n      <button onClick={() => router.push(''/contact'')}>\n        Go to Contact\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## SEO with PageLayout\n\nUse the `PageLayout` component for SEO metadata (static or dynamic):\n\n```tsx\n// Static SEO\nimport { PageLayout } from \"@/components\";\n\nexport default function AboutPage() {\n  return (\n    <PageLayout\n      title=\"About Us\"\n      description=\"Learn more about our company\"\n      keywords=\"about, company, team\"\n      canonical=\"/about\"\n    >\n      <div>About content</div>\n    </PageLayout>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// Dynamic SEO from props\nimport type { GetServerSideProps, InferGetServerSidePropsType } from \"next\";\nimport { PageLayout } from \"@/components\";\n\nexport const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async () => {\n  return {\n    props: {\n      seo: {\n        title: \"Dynamic Page\",\n        description: \"Dynamic description\",\n      },\n    },\n  };\n};\n\nexport default function DynamicPage({ seo }: InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>) {\n  return (\n    <PageLayout {...seo}>\n      <div>Content</div>\n    </PageLayout>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Always use Pages Router** - never App Router patterns\n- **Only pages handle server-side data fetching** - components, hooks, or other files should NOT make server calls\n- **Page Props type MUST be inferred** - use `InferGetServerSidePropsType<typeof getServerSideProps>` or `InferGetStaticPropsType<typeof getStaticProps>`\n- Pages are React components that export a default function\n- Data fetching functions (`getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`, `getStaticPaths`) go **after** the page component\n- Pages can use hooks like `useUsers()`, `useHotels()`, `useHotels.create()`, etc. for client-side data fetching and mutations\n- Use `PageLayout` component for SEO metadata (static or dynamic)\n- Use `useRouter` from `next/router` (not `next/navigation`)\n- Global styles go in `src/styles/globals.css` and imported in `_app.tsx`\n- TypeScript: Use `AppProps` from `next/app` for `_app.tsx`\n- The app includes `ErrorBoundary` and `QueryProvider` in `_app.tsx` - they wrap all pages automatically\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:41:09.526Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing rapid Next.js page routing and API endpoint creation.","zh":"非常适合需要快速 Next.js 页面路由和 API 端点创建的前端代理。","ja":"Next.js ページ路由と API エンドポイントの迅速な作成が必要なフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"快速한 Next.js 페이지 ルーティング 및 API 엔드ポイント 생성이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan enrutamiento de páginas Next.js rápido y creación de puntos de conexión de API.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin d''un routage de pages Next.js rapide et de création de points de terminaison d''API.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die ein schnelles Next.js-Seiten-Routing und eine API-Endpunkt-Erstellung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de roteamento de páginas Next.js rápido e criação de endpoints de API.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым требуется быстрое маршрутизация страниц Next.js и создание конечных точек API.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى توجيه صفحات Next.js السريع وإنشاء نقاط نهاية API."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create scalable and clean architectures with Next.js Pages Router, utilizing dynamic routes, API routes, and special files like _app.tsx and _document.tsx, all while leveraging TypeScript and React.","zh":"赋予代理创建可扩展和干净的架构的能力，利用 Next.js Pages Router，动态路由，API 路由和特殊文件，如 _app.tsx 和 _document.tsx，同时利用 TypeScript 和 React。","ja":"Next.js Pages Router、動的ルーティング、API ルーティング、および _app.tsx や _document.tsx などの特別なファイルを利用し、TypeScript と React を活用して、拡張可能でクリーンなアーキテクチャを作成するエージェントをエンパワーメントします。","ko":"Next.js Pages Router, 동적 라우팅, API 라우팅 및 _app.tsx, _document.tsx와 같은 특수 파일을 활용하여 확장 가능하고 깨끗한 아키텍처를 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하며,同時に TypeScript 및 React를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear arquitecturas escalables y limpias con Next.js Pages Router, utilizando rutas dinámicas, rutas de API y archivos especiales como _app.tsx y _document.tsx, aprovechando al mismo tiempo TypeScript y React.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des architectures évolutives et propres avec Next.js Pages Router, en utilisant des routes dynamiques, des routes d''API et des fichiers spéciaux comme _app.tsx et _document.tsx, tout en exploitant TypeScript et React.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare und saubere Architekturen mit Next.js Pages Router zu erstellen, indem sie dynamische Routen, API-Routen und spezielle Dateien wie _app.tsx und _document.tsx verwenden, während sie gleichzeitig TypeScript und React nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem arquiteturas escaláveis e limpas com o Next.js Pages Router, utilizando rotas dinâmicas, rotas de API e arquivos especiais como _app.tsx e _document.tsx, tudo isso aproveitando o TypeScript e o React.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать масштабируемые и чистые архитектуры с помощью Next.js Pages Router, используя динамические маршруты, маршруты API и специальные файлы, такие как _app.tsx и _document.tsx, все это при помощи TypeScript и React.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء هياكل معمارية قابلة للتحجيم وتنظيفها باستخدام Next.js Pages Router، باستخدام طرق ديناميكية وطرق API والملفات الخاصة مثل _app.tsx و _document.tsx، كل ذلك مع الاستفادة من TypeScript و React."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating dynamic page routes for user profiles","Creating RESTful API endpoints for data exchange","Building static sites with optimized routing"],"zh":["为用户配置文件生成动态页面路由","创建 RESTful API 端点用于数据交换","使用优化的路由构建静态站点"],"ja":["ユーザープロファイルの動的ページルーティングを生成する","データ交換用の RESTful API エンドポイントを作成する","最適化されたルーティングを使用して静的サイトを構築する"],"ko":["사용자 프로필을 위한 동적 페이지 라우팅 생성","데이터 교환을 위한 RESTful