مثل Hoon و Nock","مستودع متزايد من مهارات وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","حل لمشاكل ترميز الوكلاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理助手","Nock解释器","Urbit运行时","Urbit终端命令","Urbit本地编程语言","Hoon","Nock","如何使用Nock解释器","Urbit运行时教程"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Nockインタープリター","Urbitランタイム","Urbitターミナルコマンド","Urbitネイティブプログラミング言語","Hoon","Nock","Nockインタープリターの使い方","Urbitランタイムのチュートリアル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Nock 인터프리터","Urbit 런타임","Urbit 터미널 명령어","Urbit 네이티브 프로그래밍 언어","Hoon","Nock","Nock 인터프리터 사용법","Urbit 런타임 튜토리얼"],"es":["Herramientas de AI Agent","Urbit runtime","Hoon y Nock","cómo usar nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","alternativas a nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","instalación de nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","guía de configuración de nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","qué es Urbit"," Agents de codificación"],"fr":["Outils d''Agents IA","runtime d''Urbit","Hoon et Nock","comment utiliser nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","alternatives à nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","installation de nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","guide de configuration de nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","quoi est Urbit","Agents de codage"],"de":["AI-Tools","Urbit Runtime","Hoon und Nock","wie man nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant verwendet","Alternativen zu nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","Installation von nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","Konfigurationsanleitung für nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","was ist Urbit","Codierungsagenten"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","como usar Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","o que é Urbit","Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant vs outros agentes de IA","guia de instalação do Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","configuração do Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant"],"ru":["инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","как использовать Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","что такое Urbit","Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant vs другие ИИ-агенты","руководство по установке Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","настройка Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","كيفية استخدام Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","ما هو Urbit","Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant مقابل وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الآخرون","دليل تثبيت Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant","تكوين Nock Interpreter Engineer Assistant"]}},"owner":"toplyr-narfur","repo":"urbit-skills","repoPath":"toplyr-narfur/urbit-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.962Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nock-interpreter-engineer-assistant","description":"Expert Nock interpreter builder for implementing virtual machines in C, Python, Rust, Haskell, or JavaScript. Use when building Nock interpreters, porting between languages, implementing evaluation loops, or understanding Nock runtime behavior.","bodyPreview":"# Nock Interpreter Engineer\n\nExpert guidance for implementing Nock virtual machines across multiple programming languages with proper evaluation loops, tree operations, and runtime optimization.\n\n## Implementation Architecture\n\n### Core Components\n\n#### 1. Noun Representation\n**Atoms**: Natural numbers with arbitrary precision\n- **C**: GMP (GNU Multiple Precision) or custom BigInt\n- **Python**: Built-in `int` (unlimited precision)\n- **Rust**: `num-bigint` crate or `bigint` crate\n- **Haskell**: `","body":"# Nock Interpreter Engineer\n\nExpert guidance for implementing Nock virtual machines across multiple programming languages with proper evaluation loops, tree operations, and runtime optimization.\n\n## Implementation Architecture\n\n### Core Components\n\n#### 1. Noun Representation\n**Atoms**: Natural numbers with arbitrary precision\n- **C**: GMP (GNU Multiple Precision) or custom BigInt\n- **Python**: Built-in `int` (unlimited precision)\n- **Rust**: `num-bigint` crate or `bigint` crate\n- **Haskell**: `Integer` type (native)\n- **JavaScript**: `BigInt` (ES2020+)\n\n**Cells**: Ordered pairs (cons cells)\n```rust\npub enum Noun {\n    Atom(BigUint),\n    Cell(Box<Noun>, Box<Noun>),\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Parser & Printer\nParse text format to internal representation:\n```\n[a b c]        -> Cell(Atom(a), Cell(Atom(b), Atom(c)))\n123             -> Atom(123)\n[a [b c]]      -> Cell(Atom(a), Cell(Atom(b), Atom(c)))\n```\n\nPrint back to readable format.\n\n#### 3. Evaluation Loop\nPattern matching on formula opcodes (0-12):\n```python\ndef evaluate(subject, formula):\n    while True:\n        if not is_cell(formula):\n            raise NockCrash(\"formula must be cell\")\n\n        op, rest = formula\n        result = dispatch(op, subject, rest)\n        if is_crash(result):\n            return result\n        subject, formula = result, rest\n        if is_constant(formula):  # Rule 1\n            return formula\n```\n\n## Nock Rules Implementation\n\n### Rule 0: Slot (`[a b] /`)\nBinary tree addressing for efficient axis traversal:\n```\n[subject slot] / = value_at_slot\n```\n\n**Implementation**: Convert slot number to axis path (left/right sequence), traverse subject tree.\n\n### Rule 1: Constant (`[a] *`)\n```\n[subject] * = a\n```\n\nStops evaluation, returns constant `a`.\n\n### Rule 2: Evaluate (`[a b c] +`)\n```\n[subject [a b]] + = [subject a] c\n```\n\nRecurse: evaluate `a` against `subject`, then evaluate result as formula with `c`.\n\n### Rule 3: Cell Test (`[a] ?`)\n```\n[subject a] ? = 0 if a is cell, 1 if a is atom\n```\n\nType discrimination for atoms vs cells.\n\n### Rule 4: Increment (`[a] +`)\n```\n[subject a] + = a + 1\n```\n\nNatural number addition.\n\n### Rule 5: Equality (`[a b] =`)\n```\n[subject a b] = = a b\n```\n\nStructural equality: `0` if identical, `1` if different.\n\n### Rule 6-9: Composition\n- Rule 6: `[[a b] c] /` = `[[a b] / c]`\n- Rule 7: `[a b c] =` = `a b c` (three-element cell)\n- Rule 8: `[a b] +` = `a + b`\n- Rule 9: `[a b] +` = `a + b`\n\nFormulas 2-9 are composites of rules 0-5.\n\n### Rule 10: Edit (`[a b c]`)\n```\n[subject [a b c]] = nock(subject, b)\n```\nTree editing; replaces part of the subject at axis `a`.\n\n### Rule 11: Hint (`[a b]`)\n```\n[subject [a b]] = nock(subject, b)\n```\n\nOptimization hint; evaluates `b` and may use `a` as a hint to the runtime.\n\n### Rule 12: Scry (`[a b] ^`)\n```\n[subject [a b]] ^ = memory[a][b]\n```\n\nReferentially transparent read of memory slot `b` within noun `a`.\n\n## Performance Patterns\n\n### Tail Call Optimization (TCO)\n\nDetect and optimize recursive formulas:\n```python\n# Before: creates stack frames\n[subject [[a b] c]] + = ...\n\n# After: if formula ends with recursive call, reuse stack\nif ends_with_recursive_call(formula):\n    return tco_evaluate(subject, formula)\n```\n\n### Memoization\nCache evaluation results for repeated sub-formulas:\n```python\n_memo = {}\n\ndef memo_evaluate(subject, formula):\n    key = (subject, formula)\n    if key in _memo:\n        return _memo[key]\n    result = evaluate(subject, formula)\n    _memo[key] = result\n    return result\n```\n\n### Lazy Evaluation\nDefer computation until value needed:\n```python\nclass Thunk:\n    def __init__(self, subject, formula):\n        self.subject = subject\n        self.formula = formula\n        self._cached = None\n\n    def force(self):\n        if self._cached is None:\n            self._cached = evaluate(self.subject, self.formula)\n        return self._cached\n```\n\n## Language-Specific Patterns\n\n### C Implementation\n```c\ntypedef struct {\n    mpz_t atom;\n    struct Noun *cell;\n} Noun;\n\nNoun* slot(Noun* subject, Noun* axis);\nNoun* evaluate(Noun* subject, Noun* formula);\n```\n\n**Pros**: Maximum control, pointer efficiency\n**Cons**: Manual memory management, complexity\n\n### Python Implementation\n```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\nNoun = Union[int, tuple]\n\ndef evaluate(subject: Noun, formula: Noun) -> Noun:\n    if not isinstance(formula, tuple):\n        raise NockCrash(\"formula must be cell\")\n    ...\n```\n\n**Pros**: Simplicity, fast prototyping\n**Cons**: Performance overhead\n\n### Rust Implementation\n```rust\npub enum Noun {\n    Atom(BigUint),\n    Cell(Box<Noun>, Box<Noun>),\n}\n\nimpl Noun {\n    pub fn evaluate(&self, formula: &Noun) -> Result<Noun, NockCrash> {\n        match formula {\n            Noun::Cell(op, rest) => dispatch(op, self, rest),\n            _ => Ok(formula.clone()),\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Pros**: Memory safety, zero-cost abstractions\n**Cons**: Borrow checker complexity\n\n### Haskell Implementation\n```haskell\ndata Noun = Atom Integer | Cell Noun Noun\n\nevaluate :: Noun -> Noun -> Noun\nevaluate subject formula = case formula of\n    Cell (Atom 0, rest) -> slot subject rest\n    Cell (Atom 1, rest) -> rest\n    Cell (Atom 2, Cell(a, Cell(b, c))) -> evaluate (evaluate subject a) c\n    ...\n```\n\n**Pros**: Type safety, pattern matching\n**Cons**: Learning curve\n\n### JavaScript Implementation\n```javascript\nclass Noun {\n    constructor(value) {\n        this.isCell = Array.isArray(value);\n        this.value = value;\n    }\n}\n\nfunction evaluate(subject, formula) {\n    if (!formula.isCell) {\n        throw new NockCrash(\"formula must be cell\");\n    }\n    const [op, ...rest] = formula.value;\n    return dispatch(op, subject, rest);\n}\n```\n\n**Pros**: Web compatibility\n**Cons**: Performance, type safety\n\n## Testing & Validation\n\n### Reference Test: Decrement\n```python\ndef test_decrement():\n    subject = 0\n    formula = [8 [1 0] 8 [1 6 [5 [0 7]] 4 0 6] [0 6] 9 2 [0 2] [4 0 6] 0 7] 9 2 0 1]\n    result = evaluate(subject, formula)\n    assert result == 0, f\"Expected 0, got {result}\"\n```\n\n### Edge Cases\n- **Empty subject**: `[~ [1 0]]` should work\n- **Large atoms**: Test with 64-bit, 128-bit, larger\n- **Deep trees**: Stack overflow prevention\n- **Memory pressure**: Graceful handling, not crash\n\n### Benchmarking\nCompare performance against reference implementations:\n```\nImplementation | Decrement (ms) | Formula 2 (ms) | Memory (MB)\n-------------|-----------------|---------------|--------------\nPython       | 150             | 50             | 25\nRust         | 5               | 0.5            | 3\nC (GMP)     | 1               | 0.1            | 1\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### 1. Incorrect Slot Calculation\n```\nSlot 1 = axis [0 1]  // Correct\nSlot 2 = axis [1 0]  // Correct, NOT [0 1 1]\n```\n\n### 2. Missing TCO\nDeep recursion crashes stack without trampoline or TCO.\n\n### 3. Inefficient Noun Copying\nDeep clones of nouns create O(n²) behavior. Use reference counting or structural sharing.\n\n### 4. Incorrect Subject Handling\nForgetting to update `subject` after evaluation changes context.\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Nock 4K Specification](https://github.com/urbit/urbit/blob/main/pkg/arvo/sys/zuse.hoon)\n- [nock-interpreter-patterns](../nock-interpreter-patterns/SKILL.md)\n- [nock-multi-language-implementations](../nock-multi-language-implementations/SKILL.md)\n- [nock-specification-reference](../nock-specification-reference/SKILL.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:14:23.547Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing expertise in Urbit runtime, Hoon, and Nock programming languages.","zh":"适合需要精通Urbit runtime、Hoon和Nock编程语言的AI代理，如Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code。","ja":"Urbit runtime、Hoon、Nockプログラミング言語の専門知識が必要なAIエージェント、たとえばCursor、Windsurf、Claude Codeに適しています。","ko":"Urbit runtime, Hoon 및 Nock 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 전문 지식이 필요한 AI 에이전트인 Cursor, Windsurf 및 Claude Code에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan experiencia en tiempo de ejecución de Urbit, Hoon y lenguajes de programación Nock.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code ayant besoin d''expertise en runtime Urbit, Hoon et langages de programmation Nock.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die Expertenwissen in Urbit-Laufzeit, Hoon und Nock-Programmiersprachen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de expertise em tempo de execução Urbit, Hoon e linguagens de programação Nock.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, которым необходимы знания в области среды выполнения Urbit, Hoon и языков программирования Nock.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذكيين مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى خبرة في وقت تشغيل Urbit و Hoon و Nock لغات البرمجة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Nock virtual machines across multiple programming languages, including Python, Rust, and Haskell, with proper evaluation loops, tree operations, and runtime optimization using libraries like GMP, num-bigint, and bigint.","zh":"赋予代理实现跨多种编程语言（包括Python、Rust和Haskell）的Nock虚拟机的能力，具有适当的评估循环、树操作和使用GMP、num-bigint和bigint等库的运行时优化。","ja":"Python、Rust、Haskellを含む複数のプログラミング言語にわたるNock仮想マシンの実装を可能にし、適切な評価ループ、木操作、GMP、num-bigint、bigintなどのライブラリを使用したランタイム最適化を実現します。","ko":"Python, Rust 및 Haskell을 포함한 여러 프로그래밍 언어에 걸쳐 Nock 가상 머신을 구현할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며, GMP, num-bigint 및 bigint 라이브러리를 사용한 적절한 평가 루프, 트리 연산 및 런타임 최적화를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar máquinas virtuales Nock en múltiples lenguajes de programación, incluyendo Python, Rust y Haskell, con bucles de evaluación adecuados, operaciones de árbol y optimización de ejecución utilizando bibliotecas como GMP, num-bigint y bigint.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''implémenter des machines virtuelles Nock sur plusieurs langages de programmation, notamment Python, Rust et Haskell, avec des boucles d''évaluation appropriées, des opérations d''arbre et une optimisation de l''exécution à l''aide de bibliothèques comme GMP, num-bigint et bigint.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Nock-Virtuelle Maschinen über mehrere Programmiersprachen hinweg zu implementieren, einschließlich Python, Rust und Haskell, mit geeigneten Auswerteschleifen, Baumoperationen und Laufzeitoptimierung unter Verwendung von Bibliotheken wie GMP, num-bigint und bigint.","pt":"Habilita agentes a implementar máquinas virtuais Nock em várias linguagens de programação, incluindo Python, Rust e Haskell, com laços de avaliação adequados, operações de árvore e otimização de tempo de execução usando bibliotecas como GMP, num-bigint e bigint.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать виртуальные машины Nock в нескольких языках программирования, включая Python, Rust и Haskell, с правильными циклами оценки, операциями с деревьями и оптимизацией времени выполнения с использованием библиотек, таких как GMP, num-bigint и bigint.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ آلات افتراضية Nock عبر لغات برمجة متعددة، بما في ذلك Python و Rust و Haskell، مع حلقات تقييم مناسبة وعمليات شجرة وتحسين وقت تشغيل باستخدام مكتبات مثل GMP و num-bigint و bigint."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing Nock interpreters in Python with arbitrary precision using built-in int","Optimizing Nock virtual machines in Rust with num-bigint crate","Debugging Hoon and Nock code with expert guidance on Urbit terminal commands"],"zh":["在Python中使用内置int实现Nock解释器，具有任意精度","使用num-bigint箱优化Rust中的Nock虚拟机","使用Urbit终端命令的专家指导调试Hoon和Nock代码"],"ja":["Pythonでビルトインintを使用して任意精度のNockインタープリターを実装する","num-bigintクレートを使用してRustのNock仮想マシンを最適化する","Urbitターミナルコマンドの専門家のガイダンスを使用してHoonとNockコードをデバッグする"],"ko":["Python에서 내장 int를 사용하여 임의 정밀도의 Nock 인터프리터를 구현하는 것","num-bigint 크레이트를 사용하여 Rust의 Nock 가상 머신을 최적화하는 것","Urbit 터미널 명령에 대한 전문가 지침을 사용하여 Hoon 및 Nock 코드를 디버깅하는 것"],"es":["Implementar intérpretes Nock en Python con precisión arbitraria utilizando el int integrado","Optimizar máquinas virtuales Nock en Rust con la caja num-bigint","Depurar código Hoon y Nock con orientación experta sobre comandos de terminal de Urbit"],"fr":["Implémenter des interpréteurs Nock en Python avec une précision arbitraire en utilisant l''int intégré","Optimiser les machines virtuelles Nock en Rust avec la crate num-bigint","Déboguer le code Hoon et Nock avec une orientation experte sur les commandes de terminal Urbit"],"de":["Implementieren von Nock-Interpretern in Python mit beliebiger Genauigkeit unter Verwendung des integrierten int","Optimieren von Nock-Virtuellen Maschinen in Rust mit der num-bigint-Kiste","Debuggen von Hoon- und Nock-Code mit Experte-Anleitung zu Urbit-Terminalbefehlen"],"pt":["Implementação de intérpretes Nock em Python com precisão arbitrária usando int incorporado","Otimização de máquinas virtuais Nock em Rust com crate num-bigint","Depuração de código Hoon e Nock com orientação especializada em comandos de terminal Urbit"],"ru":["Реализация интерпретаторов Nock на Python с произвольной точностью с использованием встроенного int","Оптимизация виртуальных машин Nock на Rust с помощью crate num-bigint","Отладка кода Hoon и Nock с помощью экспертных рекомендаций по командам терминала Urbit"],"ar":["تنفيذ مفسّرات Nock في Python بدقة عشوائية باستخدام int المدمج","تحسين آلات افتراضية Nock في Rust مع crate num-bigint","تصحيح أخطاء رمز Hoon و Nock مع إرشادات خبيرة لأوامر 终端 Urbit"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Urbit runtime and Nock programming language","Limited to programming languages with arbitrary precision support like Python, Rust, and Haskell"],"zh":["需要理解Urbit runtime和Nock编程语言","仅限于具有任意精度支持的编程语言，例如Python、Rust和Haskell"],"ja":["UrbitランタイムとNockプログラミング言語の理解が必要","任意精度サポートを持つプログラミング言語（たとえばPython、Rust、Haskell）に限定される"],"ko":["Urbit 런타임 및 Nock 프로그래밍 언어를 이해해야 함","임의 정밀도 지원을 가진 프로그래밍 언어(예: Python, Rust, Haskell)로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del tiempo de ejecución de Urbit y del lenguaje de programación Nock","Limitado a lenguajes de programación con soporte de precisión arbitraria como Python, Rust y Haskell"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du runtime Urbit et du langage de programmation Nock","Limité aux langages de programmation avec une prise en charge de la précision arbitraire comme Python, Rust et Haskell"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Urbit-Laufzeit und die Nock-Programmiersprache","Begrenzt auf Programmiersprachen mit Unterstützung für beliebige Genauigkeit wie Python, Rust und Haskell"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do tempo de execução Urbit e da linguagem de programação Nock","Limitado a linguagens de programação com suporte a precisão arbitrária, como Python, Rust e Haskell"],"ru":["Требует понимания среды выполнения Urbit и языка программирования Nock","Ограничен языками программирования с поддержкой произвольной точности, такими как Python, Rust и Haskell"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم وقت تشغيل Urbit و لغة برمجة Nock","محدود بلغات البرمجة التي تدعم الدقة العشوائية، مثل Python و Rust و Haskell"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"a1d462af7980fa45c4f06b7e16c7825384ceaba2288988bd89187367a307d919","qualityScore":33}');
